1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,740
When you arrive in the center of stockholm you'll realize that the city is very walkable.
到了斯德哥尔摩市中心，你会发现这座城很适合步行。

2
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:08,340
The streets are wide and it's very easy to navigate around.
街道宽敞，辨认方向也很容易。

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:15,696
But it might take you a while to walk places which is why I highly recommend buying an all inclusive travel pass.
但走到各处可能挺费时间，所以作者很推荐买交通通票。

4
00:00:15,696 --> 00:00:24,120
This allows you unlimited access to the metros the local commuter trains the buses and even the boats to get you around the city.
按他的介绍，这可不限次数搭地铁、通勤火车、公交，甚至船。

5
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:29,358
To do this all you have to do is find a ticket machine follow the instructions on the screen.
只要找一台售票机，照着屏幕指示操作。

6
00:00:29,358 --> 00:00:31,740
And it will spit you out this green card.
机器就会吐出这张绿色卡片。

7
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:38,340
To use it simply tap it on one of the turnstiles and away you go it's literally that simple.
使用时在闸机上轻轻一刷，就可以进去了，就是这么简单。

8
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:44,220
You can do exactly the same thing if you've bought your tickets via the app.
如果用应用买票，也可以做同样的操作。

9
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,405
Just use your phone and the qr code it creates to let yourself in.
用手机生成的二维码，就能自己进站。

10
00:00:49,405 --> 00:00:56,440
And the transport network itself is fast efficient and virtually no different to any other mainstream european city.
交通网络本身快捷高效，和其他常见欧洲城市几乎没什么区别。

11
00:00:56,440 --> 00:01:01,999
That has excellent public transport facilities the metro stations especially are very nicely decorated.
那些城市交通设施完善，尤其这里的地铁站装饰很漂亮。

12
00:01:01,999 --> 00:01:10,020
All the signs are both in swedish and english and they're well signposted so it's almost impossible to get lost on this network.
标牌都有瑞典文和英文，指示清楚，作者觉得几乎不可能迷路。

13
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:17,703
Alternatively if you don't want to use public transport stocko is one of the most cycle friendly cities in the world.
或者不想坐公共交通，作者说这里也是很适合骑车的城市。

14
00:01:17,703 --> 00:01:22,440
There are plenty of places where you can hire a bike or an electric scooter.
很多地方可以租自行车或电动滑板车。

15
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:28,980
And use one of the hundreds of dedicated bike lanes complete with your own traffic lights to get around the city.
可走数以百计的专用自行车道，还有专属信号灯。

16
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:33,300
It's actually a fun way of seeing the city if you like that sort of thing.
如果喜欢这种方式，骑车逛城确实挺有趣。

17
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:39,240
The sightseeing buses are a decent way of seeing the city if you have a short amount of time.
如果时间短，观光巴士也是不错的看城方式。

18
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:49,663
So now that you're here and you know how to get around the place let's visit this island right here in the middle.
既然已到这里，也知道如何出行，就去中间这座岛看看。

19
00:01:49,663 --> 00:01:53,820
Where you'll find stockholm's most famous attraction the royal palace.
这里有斯德哥尔摩最著名的景点之一，王宫。

20
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:57,026
This is sweden's equivalent to buckingham palace.
作者把它比作瑞典的白金汉宫。

21
00:01:57,026 --> 00:02:03,750
As this is the current official residence of his majesty the king king carl gustav the 16 th.
这是国王的正式居所；作者提到当时的卡尔十六世·古斯塔夫。

22
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:08,805
At time of recording he is the longest reigning swedish monarch in history.
按作者录制时的说法，他是瑞典历史上在位最久的君主。

23
00:02:08,805 --> 00:02:15,367
As you can expect from any royal palace it's heavily guarded so no misbehaving whilst you're here.
和其他王宫一样，这里守卫森严，所以别在这里捣乱。

24
00:02:15,367 --> 00:02:22,638
The entry price is actually quite reasonable and you can buy your tickets here at the tickets office or online.
作者觉得门票价格合理，可以在售票处或网上买票。

25
00:02:22,638 --> 00:02:27,687
When you go inside there's many different cool things that you can see.
进去以后有很多有意思的东西可看。

26
00:02:27,687 --> 00:02:33,240
Most notably of which is the treasury which houses all the swedish crown jewels.
最值得一提的是珍宝馆，收藏着瑞典王室珍宝。

27
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:36,807
It housed the crowns orbs and scepters of former monarchs.
那里有过去君主的王冠、王权球和权杖。

28
00:02:36,807 --> 00:02:40,100
The current crowns of all the princes and princesses.
还有王子、公主们现有的王冠。

29
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:47,244
And the royal regalia that his majesty the king wears personally including the current coronation crown.
以及国王本人佩戴的礼仪饰物，包括加冕王冠。

30
00:02:47,244 --> 00:02:53,640
You'll also visit the staterooms which includes this the grand hall of state.
还可以参观国事厅室，包括这座国家大厅。

31
00:02:54,360 --> 00:03:05,070
One of the most important rooms in all of Sweden and right at the end of this is the world famous silver throne the one the king actually sits on.
作者说这是瑞典很重要的房间，尽头就是国王所坐的著名银王座。

32
00:03:05,070 --> 00:03:13,365
You'll go through various halls especially this one that's got the coat of arms of all the raiding monarchs in the world.
还会经过各个大厅，这一间有世界各国君主的纹章。

33
00:03:13,365 --> 00:03:22,487
Including our very own king charles and if you don't know much about swedish history or the royal family you'll certainly learn a lot here.
包括他们的查尔斯国王。如果不熟悉瑞典历史或王室，在这里能学到不少。

34
00:03:22,487 --> 00:03:27,480
It's very mesmerizing to see what sort of regalia they wear for different functions.
看看不同仪式上穿戴什么礼仪服饰，作者觉得很引人入胜。
